{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1425","published":"2026-11-23T20:01:46.351Z","modified":"2026-11-23T20:15:05.539217147Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-53793","EUVD-2026-58101"],"details":"rsync before 3.5.0 contains a path confinement bypass vulnerability that allows remote clients to escape the intended inner-module root confinement by constructing paths that resolve outside the chroot boundary when the module root contains a /./ boundary marker. Attackers can exploit improper handling of the /./ notation or forge delta-basis transfers referencing xname paths that cross the /./ boundary to gain unauthorized read or write access to files outside the module's subtree.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/rsync_jll?uuid=191d6b87-264a-55f5-a0e2-c8fbce9a1ce0"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.5.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1425.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/releases/tag/v3.5.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/security/advisories/GHSA-wj7w-vh23-mm44"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rsync-path-confinement-bypass-via-boundary-marker-in-chroot-mode"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"samba:rsync":["< 3.5.0"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53793","id":"CVE-2026-53793","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:04.994Z","modified":"2026-11-06T16:00:34.757Z","published":"2026-08-13T15:19:43.690Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-53793"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-58101","id":"EUVD-2026-58101","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:06.499Z","modified":"2026-08-14T16:50:10Z","published":"2026-08-13T14:38:42Z","url":"https://euvdservices.enisa.eur